        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 141.57,
          "end": 145.11,
          "en": "we can see what's inside of that constraints object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 145.11,
          "end": 148.89,
          "en": "Because this constraints object is all about telling us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 148.89,
          "end": 152.46,
          "en": "which constraints are applied by the parent widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 152.46,
          "end": 154.95,
          "en": "in which we use this widget here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 154.95,
          "end": 157.383,
          "en": "so the parent widget of the new expense widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 158.31,
          "end": 160.38,
          "en": "And this constraints object tells us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 160.38,
          "end": 162.81,
          "en": "the minimum amount of width we can use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 162.81,
          "end": 165.39,
          "en": "and the maximum amount of width we can use,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 165.39,
          "end": 169.59,
          "en": "and then the same for the height, min height and max height.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 169.59,
          "end": 172.53300000000002,
          "en": "So if I save this and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 173.64,
          "end": 176.37,
          "en": "you will see that as I open this modal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 176.37,
          "end": 180.3,
          "en": "and I opened that debug console, I see the values here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 180.3,
          "end": 182.58,
          "en": "And here I actually only have three values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 182.58,
          "end": 185.67,
          "en": "because for min and max width it's the same value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 185.67,
          "end": 188.313,
          "en": "I have that fixed without any choice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 189.54,
          "end": 192.81,
          "en": "Now, how can these values be helpful?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 192.81,
          "end": 194.97,
          "en": "Well, with them you know exactly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 194.97,
          "end": 196.8,
          "en": "how much space you have available,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 196.8,
          "end": 200.28,
          "en": "and you can then decide which layout should be rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 200.28,
          "end": 203.19,
          "en": "And this, for example, allows you to build a widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 203.19,
          "end": 206.67000000000002,
          "en": "that can be used anywhere in your widget tree,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 206.67000000000002,
          "end": 209.25,
          "en": "and it does not care about the available width",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 209.25,
          "end": 210.99,
          "en": "or height of the screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 210.99,
          "end": 213.9,
          "en": "it does not care about the screen orientation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 213.9,
          "end": 217.26,
          "en": "but it only cares how much width and height is available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 217.26,
          "end": 219.243,
          "en": "to this specific widget here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 220.35,
          "end": 222.87,
          "en": "Now of course here, for this new expense widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 222.87,
          "end": 224.7,
          "en": "since it is inside of that modal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 224.7,
          "end": 226.95,
          "en": "it is essentially the screen dimensions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 226.95,
          "end": 228.96,
          "en": "that are available to us here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 228.96,
          "end": 231.42000000000002,
          "en": "It's the width and height of the screen, essentially.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 231.42000000000002,
          "end": 234.03,
          "en": "So therefore we could also just use MediaQuery,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 234.03,
          "end": 237.21,
          "en": "which does give us the screen width and height.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 237.21,
          "end": 239.85,
          "en": "But we could now also use the new expense widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 239.85,
          "end": 242.46,
          "en": "anywhere else in our widget tree,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 242.46,
          "end": 245.28,
          "en": "and it would only care about the constraints set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 245.28,
          "end": 247.56,
          "en": "by the parent widget, it would not care",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 247.56,
          "end": 250.62,
          "en": "about the available screen width or height.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 250.62,
          "end": 252.72,
          "en": "And we can then use this information here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 252.72,
          "end": 255.3,
          "en": "to dynamically change our layout.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 255.3,
          "end": 256.44,
          "en": "So for example here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 256.44,
          "end": 259.68,
          "en": "we could store the maximum amount of width",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 259.68,
          "end": 263.28,
          "en": "that we can use in a width variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 263.28,
          "end": 265.05,
          "en": "and now use that variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 265.05,
          "end": 268.59,
          "en": "just as we used variable here in expenses.dart",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 268.59,
          "end": 270.99,
          "en": "to render a different combination of widgets",
